    "overview": "Write, revise and publish a personal essay about a moment after which you saw something differently.",
    "prompt": "All semester we have read about thresholds: moments after which a person sees differently and cannot go back. Write a personal essay about a threshold of your own. It can be large or small: a conversation, a mistake, a first time, a loss, a discovery. Open inside a specific moment. Sequence the events so they build toward the turn. Use dialogue, pacing, telling details and sensory language. End with reflection that shows how your understanding changed, without stating a moral. Revise in at least two passes (structure, then detail) before you submit. You choose what to share; your story does not need to be dramatic to be powerful.",
