nly that Juliet is dead. He buys poison, returns to her tomb, kills Paris there, drinks the poison and dies beside her. Juliet wakes, sees Romeo dead, and stabs herself with his dagger. The families arrive, learn the whole story from the Friar, and finally make peace over their children's bodies.",
