      "body": "The rich inheritance of justice, liberty, prosperity and independence, bequeathed by your fathers, is shared by you, not by me.\n\nWhat, to the American slave, is your 4th of July? I answer: a day that reveals to him, more than all other days in the year, the gross injustice and cruelty to which he is the constant victim.\n\nFrom near the end of the speech:\nI do not despair of this country.",
      "id": "douglass-fourth-of-july-excerpt",
